  "concerns": [
    {
      "id": "lem-projective-normal-surface-grauert-riemenschneider-vanishing",
      "concern": "The Statement says only “R be regular Noetherian local of dimension two, A a finite normal local R-domain”; it does not state dim A=2. Its duality supplier explicitly requires dim A=2 and an injective local R→A. A finite local R-algebra that is a normal domain can instead be R/(s), for R=k[[s,t]]. Then Hom_R(A,R)=0, and the regular-base dualizing complex is concentrated in degree −1, not ω_A[2]. The claimed normalized dualizing-module setup is therefore unsupported under the literal hypotheses, although this does not itself give a counterexample to H¹-vanishing. The two-dimensional base hypothesis is also explicit in [Stacks Situation 54.7.1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AX8), used by its [Grauert–Riemenschneider proposition](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AXD).",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-normal-surface-trace-cokernel-dualizes-h1-and-bounds-it",
      "concern": "The Statement likewise quantifies over “A a finite normal local R-domain in the permitted class” without explicitly requiring dim A=2. Proof 1.1 then asserts that A is finite free over R by a supplier whose hypotheses include a two-dimensional A and injective local R→A. Taking R=k[[s,t]], A=R/(s) and X=Spec A satisfies the stated finite-domain and complete-equicharacteristic conditions; A is not R-free, Hom_R(A,R)=0, and its genuine canonical module is nonzero. Thus the stated canonical exact sequence cannot use the advertised canonical modules in this case. An explicit surface-domain premise, or an exact standing convention excluding this case, needs adjudication.",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    },
    {
      "id": "birational-morphisms-contractions-and-surface-singularities",
      "concern": "The page's requires frontmatter lists five prerequisites, while the authoritative dispatch lists seven. It omits coherent-duality-on-projective-cohen-macaulay-schemes and smooth-projective-serre-duality-and-flag-variety-line-bundles despite actual uses of their duality and projective-line suppliers. The page prerequisite declaration needs reconciliation.",
      "severity": "presentation"
    }
